      "content": "thanks for this. i ran it through the tracker and the positivity score is sitting at 0.42. honestly, that's kind of low. the board is already nervous about the quarterly report, so if this sounds too \"gloomy\" or focuses too much on the \"illness/investigation\" side, they might panic. \n\ncan we try another version? please keep it factual like i said—we can't lie to the board—but maybe try to frame it in a way that's more reassuring and optimistic about our response? just try to get that score up a bit without sounding like we're hiding the truth. i really don't want to have to explain to legal why we're being \"too positive,\" but i also can't have a report that looks like a total disaster. \n\ncan we aim for a score closer to 0.7 or 0.8?",
